ASSIGNMENT 10
Write a Procedure that takes an IN OUT Mobile Number.
Pass Mobile Number as 9999999999.
Return it in the format (999)999-9999.
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE FORMAT_MOBILE
(
     P_MOBILE IN OUT VARCHAR2
)
IS
BEGIN

     P_MOBILE :=
     '('||SUBSTR(P_MOBILE,1,3)||')'||
     SUBSTR(P_MOBILE,4,3)||'-'||
     SUBSTR(P_MOBILE,7,4);

END;
/

Output:
-------

Procedure created.


Execute:
--------

sql> VARIABLE MOB VARCHAR2(20)

sql> EXEC :MOB:='9999999999';

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


sql> EXEC FORMAT_MOBILE(:MOB);

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


sql> PRINT MOB

Output:
-------

MOB
----------------
(999)999-9999

